Hello all,

  Got DU 4.0D running on a Alpha Station 200 4/233.  The
graphics card is the S3 based 9FX Vision 330.  I use a Viewsonic 815 21
inch monitor.    The Xserver runs fine at 1024 x 768.  However, when I
attempt to modify the /var/dt/Xservers file to specifiy a higher
resolution,  the monitor cannot sync, and indicates "no signal".   I use
the following entry in the Xservers file:

  :0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -screen0 1280 -vsync 72 :0

Both the video card and the monitor are 1280x1024 capable.  I've
specified a -vsync of 60,66,72,75 with similar results.   I've looked at
the man page for Xdec and find that the -vsync parameter is
undocumented.   

Are there other parameters that I might use to control the signal?   Has
anyone else managed to get this configuration ( or similar ) to work in
1280x1024?  

Sizer info after mods to Xserver:

# sizer -c
cpu             "DEC2100_A50"
# sizer -v
Digital UNIX V4.0D  (Rev. 878); Mon Dec 21 21:52:11 PST 1998
# sizer -wt
14
# sizer -wu
1
# sizer -gt
S3TRIO
# sizer -gr
1280x1024


  
