We have a strange problem with our fontserver (xfs from X11R5). Once in a
while
it starts delivering disorted fonts for some but not all fonts (they look
like chinese).

Apparantly it happens at random - i runs happily for a few days - and then
out of the
blue the problem arises. Momentarily, the problem is solved by simply
restarting the
font server - just to reappear at a later time.

Apart from restarting messages, the only stamps that makes it into the
error file
are:

/usr/bin/X11/xfs notice: Reusing existing file descriptor 3                
    
/usr/bin/X11/xfs notice: Reusing existing file descriptor 4                
    
/usr/bin/X11/xfs notice: resetting                                         
    

with the latter coming from a font server restart. It is difficult to tell
when the problem
occurs relative to the log notices, since the fontserver do not add a time
stamp.(if you try to add them yourself f. inst. using the crontab, it will
sort the lines in the log and
