> you should give the option  -lfor  (or -lf2c for Linux)  in order to
> link Fortran routines correctly.

Good suggestion, but not always literaly true. The point is that if you do
not link with the fortran linker (probably f77 or f90 for you) you do not get
automatic acceess to the Fortran system library and you need to link them by
hand. On my system they are libf.a, hence you need -lf Otherwise you can link
with the Fortran linker and link by hand the c routines -lc.

