In article <F5EqED.7AA@wlbr.iipo.gtegsc.com>, "Karl Shepherd"
<karl.shepherd@gsc.gte.com> wrote:

>I would like to use a Digital DMCC workstation and its serial port as the
>terminal for the console port on another Digital workstation.  Does anyone
>know of some SW, that runs on Digital UNIX 4.0d/e, that could be used as
>terminal emulator program and communicate through the workstation serial
>port?

        'tip'
        see the man page
        Just add an entry to /etc/remote along the lines of:

                mumble_name:dv=/dev/tty00:br#9600:pa=none

        then enter the command:

                tip mumble_name

        Your milage may vary and you may need to modify some of the
/etc/remote fields to suit your environment.  Again see the tip man page.

