The solution will depend very much on the exact nature of your hardware and
the details of error that you get.

If it is any use I have had a similar experience when trying to reboot an
alpha server 4100.  The boot up tests ran successfully but could not load
the OS as it could not find /osf_boot.

Tha answer in this case was to identify the CD-ROM device using show dev
from the >>> prompt, load the operating system CD and boot from that.

When prompted enter the Unix Shell.
mount the root disk on /mnt then copy the /osf_boot file from / to /mnt.

Then reboot this time from the root device.

This worked for me as it was merely a matter of getting the system up and
recovering the /osf_boot file.  It may be entirely inappropriate for you,
but  you never know.

It would certainly be a good first step to boot of your Operating System
Media and then go from there.

Regards

Richard





